---

# Current Progress Update

At this stage of the project, the SIR equations and both numerical solvers have been implemented successfully. Euler’s Method and RK4 simulations are producing epidemic curves and comparison plots.

One challenge was making the numerical solvers flexible enough to test different parameter values and timestep sizes. Initially, the code structure was too limited and difficult to reuse for multiple simulations. This was improved by turning the solvers into reusable functions with adjustable parameters.

Another challenge involved numerical stability, particularly for Euler’s Method when larger timestep sizes were used. Testing smaller timestep values improved the accuracy and smoothness of the solutions.

Current visualizations include:

* SIR population trajectories
* Euler vs RK4 comparison graphs
* peak infection calculations
* heatmap inspired visualizations

